Use io and list.

Define function permute taking nums as a pointer to List of whole number, start as an unsigned number, n as an unsigned number:
    If start equals n:
        For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to n - 1:
            Say list_get(nums, i).
        Say "---".
        Give back.
    For every i from start to n - 1:
        Let temporary be list_get(nums, start).
        list_set(nums, start, list_get(nums, i)).
        list_set(nums, i, temporary).
        permute(nums, start + 1, n).
        Set temporary to list_get(nums, start).
        list_set(nums, start, list_get(nums, i)).
        list_set(nums, i, temporary).
Done.

Let nums be a list of 1, 2, and 3.
Let n be count of nums.
permute(address of nums, 0, n).
list_free(address of nums).
Return 0.
